<title>BELGIUM: EU to vote on Canadian quality wheat import quota.</title>
<headline>EU to vote on Canadian quality wheat import quota.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's cereals management committee is due to vote on Thursday on a draft regulation allowing an additional quality wheat import quota for Canada, an EU official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The 300,000 additional quality wheat quota is part of a GATT concession compensating for the enlargement of the EU under article 24/6.</p>
<p>&quot;The draft regulation on Canadian quality wheat imports will be discussed at an experts meeting before the management committee where a vote is scheduled,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The management committee is also due to vote on a draft regulation amending the import tariff for Argentine flint maize.</p>
<p>&quot;Otherwise the meeting is listed as routine,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
